WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.392
Apple checks the pixel size of every screenshot

2
00:00:02.438 --> 00:00:05.178
you upload, exactly. Get it wrong and your

3
00:00:05.224 --> 00:00:08.034
submission bounces. So start by dropping your

4
00:00:08.081 --> 00:00:10.739
screenshots in — straight from the simulator,

5
00:00:10.762 --> 00:00:12.736
as many as you like, and they stay in

6
00:00:12.771 --> 00:00:13.908
the order you picked them.

7
00:00:14.350 --> 00:00:15.661
Now choose your target.

8
00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:18.274
Every slot here comes from Apple's and Google's

9
00:00:18.332 --> 00:00:20.062
own published specifications,

10
00:00:20.271 --> 00:00:21.873
with the exact pixel size,

11
00:00:21.989 --> 00:00:23.336
which devices it covers,

12
00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:25.646
and whether it is actually required or just

13
00:00:25.704 --> 00:00:28.979
optional. Some slots accept more than one size,

14
00:00:29.048 --> 00:00:30.290
so pick the one you need.

15
00:00:30.894 --> 00:00:32.334
Add a headline for the slide,

16
00:00:32.392 --> 00:00:34.006
above the device or below it.

17
00:00:34.447 --> 00:00:36.920
Choose a background — a preset gradient,

18
00:00:37.013 --> 00:00:40.008
or your own colours. Turn the device frame

19
00:00:40.054 --> 00:00:41.959
on if you want one; it is drawn with

20
00:00:42.005 --> 00:00:44.211
canvas shapes, so there is no device photo

21
00:00:44.269 --> 00:00:46.673
in your output. Then export.

22
00:00:46.916 --> 00:00:50.016
JPEG by default, because a canvas PNG always

23
00:00:50.063 --> 00:00:52.129
carries an alpha channel and Apple rejects

24
00:00:52.164 --> 00:00:54.312
those. Nothing was uploaded,

25
00:00:54.428 --> 00:00:56.007
and there is no watermark.
